===Etymology===
{{L.}} [[post]], ''[[afterwards]]'' + [[mortem]] from [[mors]], ''[[death]]''

===Adjective===
'''[[post]] [[mortem]]'''

# occurring after [[death]]
#:''The injuries were found to have been caused '''post-mortem'''.''

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[post]] [[mortem]]}} (abbreviated as ''[[PM]]'')

# An [[investigation]] of a [[corpse]] to determine the cause of [[death]]; an [[autopsy]]
# {{figurative}} Any investigation after something considered unsucessfull, especially used of meetings and bridge games.

